XR screen: the room's ambience around the giant screen (WakerQuest's mode pantalla, ambient)

The game draws its ambient actors a second time for the room (the view delta taking the game camera's
view space to the head's), marked with GX_AURORA_SET_AMBIENT (AuroraSetAmbient): DrawData.ambient,
and its render pass hasAmbient. Those draws are left out of the frame's picture (and of the stereo
right eye's). After the frame, when aurora_xr_set_ambient is on and nothing is drawn over the screen
(ImGui): the screen's picture kept aside (the EFB, or the right eye's in stereo; the left eye's is
stereo's copy), then for each eye the passes with ambient draws over a cleared EFB, those alone (no
clears, palette conversions, copies, snapshots nor resolves), with the diorama's eye shift, each
masked (the mask's fourth shape, fade[3] 3): alpha 0 where the line from the eye crosses the screen's
rectangle, fading out away from it, 0 where nothing was drawn. The buffer is then the screen's eye(s)
and the ambience's left and right eyes (AuroraXrFrame.ambient, tag: the head pose they were drawn
for), for a projection layer over the screen. Off (never called), nothing changes.
